# The Waveshare ESP32-S3-Touch-LCD-1.69 (this fork, 2026-10-17): layered over
# sdkconfig.defaults, as the Touch-LCD-2's file is. ESP32-S3R8 - 16 MB flash
# and 8 MB octal PSRAM - with a 1.69" ST7789V2 IPS (240 x 280 with rounded
# corners, scanned landscape 280 x 240), a CST816T touch panel with its own
# reset line, a QMI8658 IMU, a PCF85063 RTC and a passive buzzer. No codec,
# no PMIC: the audio port is the stub; the RTC is read at boot as on every
# board. Phase 2 (battery): the meter reads VBAT through the ADC
# (battery_port_adc.c, GPIO 1), app_main latches SYS_EN (GPIO 41) first of
# all, the PWR key (GPIO 40) sleeps on a short press and powers off on a
# 1.5 s hold, and the buzzer (GPIO 42) is held low (board_pins.h,
# board_power.c).
#
#   tools/build_wst169.sh            # build into build_wst169/
#   idf.py -B build_wst169 -D SDKCONFIG=build_wst169/sdkconfig \
#          -D SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.defaults.wst169" build
CONFIG_POCKET_TANK_WST169=y
CONFIG_POCKET_TANK_DISPLAY_SH8601=n
CONFIG_POCKET_TANK_DISPLAY_ST7789=y
CONFIG_POCKET_TANK_TOUCH_FT3168=y
CONFIG_POCKET_TANK_AUDIO_ES8311=n
# The QMI8658 senses handling (the tank light) but does not turn the picture,
# as on the Touch-LCD-2: its axes on this board are not measured yet. The
# settings page's SCREEN row sets which way up the picture is.
CONFIG_POCKET_TANK_IMU_QMI8658=y
CONFIG_POCKET_TANK_IMU_MPU6050=n
CONFIG_POCKET_TANK_IMU_AUTO_FLIP=n
# Sleep goes dark and light-sleeps, never deep, as the Touch-LCD-2's does: a
# touch or a pick-up lights it again where it was. Only the factory default:
# the settings page's SLEEP row changes it at run time (NVS tank/sleep).
CONFIG_POCKET_TANK_SLEEP_LIGHT=y
